From 174ddf5f3f4116b76cfb94f8b0f51f55e207091c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cm4-module <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:28:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Regional fallback: check new vias against
 pass-through-only board obstacles

The fallback opens its region to every layer and relies on board obstacles to
limit layer transitions, but only movable preloaded vias were checked. The
intra-node solvers see obstacles on the layers they route on, so obstacles
that lie only on layers a via passes through (an inner keep-out) were never
checked and vias landed inside them. Check those for every new route, count
rejections separately, and use the obstacle margin when the SRJ gives no
via-to-pad rule instead of skipping the check.
